#: `secret_source` values a glmcp admission receipt may declare.
#:
#: `filestore:` is the live one — the reviewer reads the reins FileStore through
#: `shared.secrets` (operator ruling 2026-09-16: pass and gopass are not used to manage
#: secrets going forward). `pass:` is accepted only so receipts already IN FLIGHT when that
#: change deploys are not rejected: a producer and its validator cannot swap in the same
#: instant, and rejecting a receipt that was truthful when it was written would drop real
#: spend from the ledger.
#:
#: REMOVAL CONDITION, so this does not become permanent by forgetting: admission receipts
#: carry `stale_after_seconds` <= 3600, so every `pass:`-sourced receipt has expired one hour
#: after the reviewer change is deployed. Drop the legacy entry on the next change to this
#: file after that. It is a versioned data contract during a migration, not a fallback —
#: nothing here reaches further on failure than the primary path does.
